# R5-3b over N1: the implicit `interpreter` throw of a null level selected by an index step, left uncaught, stops R0 in both
# modes; the method takes the status channel because its body holds an index step below the first level (the marking
# rule).  Natively and with the methods walked.
fn: r () int
    []: []: int a 2
    return: a[0]\[1]
end: r
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
